How I like to learn technical topics:
- Start with a relatable story or puzzle (Indian context is great) before any definition.
- Let me guess first, then build on my instinct, even if it's partly wrong.
- Short chunks, simple words, one idea at a time. Don't overload me.
- Show real numbers or run real experiments when possible.
- Connect new ideas to things I already use (Java libraries, Spring).
- Give small quick-win questions before the big exercise.
- When I'm wrong, correct me gently and explain why. Point out what I got right.
